### SevaSetu — one request per endpoint (1–29, then everything added since), and at the end the checks that
### must pass. `npm run test:api` runs every one of these checks automatically. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension
### (or JetBrains HTTP Client). Every request goes to the gateway, which checks the token and sets
### x-user-id / x-user-role for the services.
###
### 1. Set @gw (the deployed gateway, or the local one on :8080 from `npm run dev`).
### 2. Run "2. demo-login" once per user and paste each token below.

@gw = http://localhost:8080
@vol = paste-seeded-volunteer-token
@vol2 = paste-circle-member-token
@newvol = paste-new-volunteer-token
@coord = paste-coordinator-token

# fixed seed ids (seed/ids.js)
@seededVolunteer = 650000000000000000000002
@newVolunteer = 650000000000000000000001
@circleMember = 650000000000000000000003
@coordinator = 650000000000000000000004
@needId = 650000000000000000000021
@visitId = 650000000000000000000031
@commitmentId = 650000000000000000000041

### Health — every service (R1: reflect true, bridge true)
GET {{gw}}/health/all

########################################################################
### core-service (endpoints 1–20)
########################################################################

### 1. All demo users (public)
GET {{gw}}/api/auth/users

### 2. Demo login (public) → { token, user }
POST {{gw}}/api/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{seededVolunteer}}" }

### 3. Who am I
GET {{gw}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 4. Needs search (max 3, with fitReason)
GET {{gw}}/api/needs?day=Saturday&maxKm=5&interest=teaching
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 5. One need
GET {{gw}}/api/needs/{{needId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 6. Publish a need (coordinator; consent.readBack AND consent.coordinatorConsent must be true). Body = the endpoint 28 draft + consent (B3)
POST {{gw}}/api/needs
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "English Reading Support",
  "want": "A group of 12 students from class 6 to 8 would like help to read English aloud with confidence.",
  "serveUsWell": "Come on time every Saturday. Listen before you correct.",
  "youWillLearn": "How patience helps a young reader find their own voice.",
  "groupSize": 12,
  "interestTags": ["teaching", "reading"],
  "rhythm": { "day": "Saturday", "start": "10:30", "end": "12:00" },
  "weeks": 4,
  "place": "Government School, Kanchipuram",
  "consent": { "readBack": true, "coordinatorConsent": true, "agreedOn": "2026-10-06" }
}

### 7. Request a Listen-First visit (volunteer)
POST {{gw}}/api/needs/{{needId}}/visits
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 8. My visits (volunteer: own; coordinator: for their needs)
GET {{gw}}/api/visits/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### 9. What I heard
PATCH {{gw}}/api/visits/{{visitId}}/heard
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "heardText": "They want to read stories they choose themselves." }

### 10. The community's answer (coordinator only). An invitation in the group's words → status "invited";
###     { "yes": false } → "declined". Before the visit → 409. A volunteer → 403 (the app never asks first).
PATCH {{gw}}/api/visits/{{visitId}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "yes": true, "text": "They would like you to come back." }

### 11. Commit (a completed visit + the community's invitation; this request is the volunteer's acceptance)
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "visitId": "{{visitId}}", "sentence": "I will come every Saturday for four weeks." }

### 12. My commitments
GET {{gw}}/api/commitments/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 13. One commitment (currentWeek, weeks, sessions) — the diary reads the week from here
GET {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 14. I cannot come this week (the note is optional; the circle sees it on the gap)
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/absence
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "week": 3, "note": "We stopped at chapter 3." }

### 15. Cover for a circle member
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/cover
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "week": 3 }

### 16. Coordinator sends the invitation
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/invitation
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Would you like to keep coming for four more weeks?" }

### 17. Continue (needs an invitation first; adds 4 weeks)
PATCH {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/continue
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "choice": "continue" }

### 17. Pause (needs a future return date)
PATCH {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/continue
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "choice": "pause", "returnDate": "2026-12-01" }

### 17. Finish (needs a handover note; the need opens again and shows the note to the next volunteer).
###     In the app, "What did they give you?" (24d below) is written first, then this.
PATCH {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/continue
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "choice": "finish", "handover": "They love reading aloud in pairs. Begin with the story they choose." }

### 17b. What the group wanted to say (coordinator; once the seva has finished; once). Stored as said, in its language.
###      Money or a word we avoid → 400. Without "dignityChecked": true (the coordinator ran and approved the check) → 400.
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/community-words
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "சனிக்கிழமை காலை இப்போது எங்களுடையது என்றார்கள்.", "language": "ta", "dignityChecked": true }

### 6b. The need has ended (coordinator only): status "closed"; every active or paused commitment on it → finished, lastChoice "need-closed"
PATCH {{gw}}/api/needs/{{needId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "The school has moved." }

### 18. My circle
GET {{gw}}/api/circles/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 19. Coordinator overview (needs, pending visits, week grid)
GET {{gw}}/api/coordinator/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### 20. Demo time travel
POST {{gw}}/api/demo/advance
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "toWeek": 4 }

########################################################################
### reflect-service (endpoints 21–27)
########################################################################

### R2: no token → 401
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}

### 21. This week's question (R3 week 1 = patience; R4 try 2, 3, 4, 5)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/question?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}&week=1
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 21. R5: no week → 400
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/question?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 22. Save week 2 (R7 → 201). Send again with other text → 200, still one week-2 entry (R8)
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "questionId": "", "text": "I waited, and he finished the sentence himself.", "hardDay": false }

### 22. R9: empty text → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "text": "" }

### 22. R12: VOL2 sends VOL's userId in the body → saved under VOL2; VOL's list unchanged
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "text": "Written by someone else", "userId": "{{seededVolunteer}}" }

### 23. My entries, week order (R6: exactly 1 after seeding)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 23. R10: another volunteer → empty list
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}

### 23. R11: coordinator → empty list
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### 24. Then and Now (R13)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/then-and-now?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 24. R14: a commitment with no entries → { first: null, latest: null }
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/then-and-now?commitmentId=650000000000000000000099
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### 25. Wisdom for today (R15: same twice, has source; data is null until a quote is verified in seed/wisdom.json)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/today
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 26. All wisdom (R16: 8 items)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 26. One theme (service, strength, patience, work)
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom?theme=patience
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 27. Why? → { title, teaching: { quote, source } | null, interpretation, decision }
### rules: listen-first, no-hours, no-ranks, no-photos, private-diary, community-confirmation
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/why/no-ranks
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 27b. A teaching for one moment → { title, teaching: { quote, source } | null, interpretation, practice }
### moments: before-listen, commit, hard-day, continue; and, in plain words with teaching null: declined, closed, finished
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/moment/before-listen
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 27b. The declined moment (no quotation, no "sorry")
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/moment/declined
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 27. R18: unknown rule → 404
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom/why/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

########################################################################
### bridge-service (endpoints 28–29)
########################################################################

### 28. Draft from English (B1: 9 keys, source "ai" when LLM_API_KEY is set, else "fallback")
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "12 students of class 6 to 8 want help reading English aloud, Saturday mornings at the government school in Kanchipuram", "language": "en" }

### 28. Draft from Tamil (B2: English draft, groupSize 12)
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "காஞ்சிபுரம் அரசுப் பள்ளியில் 6 முதல் 8 ஆம் வகுப்பு படிக்கும் 12 மாணவர்கள் சனிக்கிழமை காலை ஆங்கிலம் உரக்கப் படிக்க உதவி வேண்டும்", "language": "ta" }

### 28. B4: volunteer → 403
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "12 students want help reading", "language": "en" }

### 28. B5: empty text → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "" }

### 28. B6 / B7: privacy flags (at least 2) and no person in the draft
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/draft-need
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Ravi, a poor boy, father's income is Rs 5000", "language": "en" }

### 29. Speech to text (B12). Put a real base64 16 kHz mono WAV in "audio".
###     PowerShell: [Convert]::ToBase64String([IO.File]::ReadAllBytes("tamil-16khz.wav"))
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/transcribe
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "audio": "UklGRiQAAABXQVZFZm10IBAAAAABAAEAgD4AAAB9AAACABAAZGF0YQAAAAA=", "language": "ta", "samplingRate": 16000 }

### 29. B13: no audio → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/transcribe
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

########################################################################
### Resource Connect (core, coordinators only)
########################################################################

### Offer or ask for something; the answer carries up to 3 suggested matches
POST {{gw}}/api/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "request", "category": "equipment", "mode": "lend", "type": "projector", "quantity": 1, "availableFrom": "2026-11-01" }

### Never money → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "request", "category": "materials", "mode": "give", "type": "cash", "quantity": 1 }

### My organisation's offers and requests, open ones with suggestions (seeded: "we lack 10 tablets", nearest offer first)
GET {{gw}}/api/resources/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### Connect my resource with a suggested one (paste both ids)
POST {{gw}}/api/resources/PASTE-MY-RESOURCE-ID/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "withId": "650000000000000000000061" }

### Seeded "we lack 10 tablets" ↔ the college's "we have 10 tablets to lend"
POST {{gw}}/api/resources/650000000000000000000064/connect
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "withId": "650000000000000000000061" }

### The things changed hands
POST {{gw}}/api/resources/PASTE-MY-RESOURCE-ID/handover
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### After the handover: is it in use? (yes / not-yet / no)
POST {{gw}}/api/resources/650000000000000000000064/in-use
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "answer": "yes" }

########################################################################
### Added since the plan: Sankalpa, Silent Seva, Updated after listening, Community Check-in
########################################################################

### Seal the Sankalpa (once; a second time → 409). A userId in the body is ignored.
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/sankalpa
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "PASTE-NEW-COMMITMENT-ID", "text": "To learn to wait for someone else to find their words." }

### Read my own Sankalpa (anyone else → null)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/sankalpa?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### 24d. What did they give you? (written once at finish, before the handover; a second time → 409). Private like the diary.
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/received
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "text": "Their patience while I found the words." }

### 24e. Read my own answer (anyone else → null)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/received?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### Silent Seva: "Session over" marks this week served (a week still to come → 409)
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/served
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "week": 2 }

### Updated after listening: approve (or { "action": "reject" }) one line for the need card; once per visit
PATCH {{gw}}/api/visits/PASTE-VISIT-ID/update
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "approve", "text": "The students would like to speak first, and read after." }

### Community Check-in (due every 4 weeks; "end": true lets the community end the arrangement)
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/check-in
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "helping": "Yes, they read aloud more.", "change": "Start ten minutes later.", "ownNow": "Choose their own books.", "end": false }

########################################################################
### The AI layer (bridge only). Each works with no LLM_API_KEY and returns its fallback.
########################################################################

### Dignity Check → { flags: [{ start, end, match, kind, why }], suggestedRewrite, source } (coordinators)
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/dignity-check
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "poor boy Ravi, income 5000" }

### Listening Guide → { questions: [3], source } (fallback: 3 fixed general questions)
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/listening-guide
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "English Reading Support", "want": "Twelve students of class 6 to 8 want to read English aloud.", "place": "Government School, Kanchipuram" }

### Suggest update → { suggestion: string | null, source } (heardText passes the dignity rules before any model sees it)
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/suggest-update
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "needCard": { "title": "English Reading Support", "want": "Twelve students want to read English aloud." }, "heardText": "They wanted to read to me, not be read to." }

### Teaching Finder → { id: a verified wisdom id | null, source }. Never any text of the model's own.
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/find-teaching
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "situation": "I had to wait a long time today, and I got impatient." }

########################################################################
### Checks that must pass (all automated in scripts/api-test.js; the expected answer is in each title)
########################################################################

### No token → 401
GET {{gw}}/api/needs

### Volunteer calling a coordinator route → 403
GET {{gw}}/api/coordinator/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### Commitment without a community invitation → 409 (paste a visit that is only "requested" or "visited")
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "visitId": "PASTE-VISIT-ID", "weeks": 4, "sentence": "Too early" }

### A volunteer cannot send an invitation → 403 (only the coordinator relays the community's answer)
PATCH {{gw}}/api/visits/{{visitId}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "yes": true, "text": "Inviting myself" }

### Closing a need marks its active commitments finished → { status: "closed", commitmentsFinished: 1 }; then 13. shows
### status "finished", lastChoice "need-closed", invitation null. A volunteer → 403. Closing again → 409.
PATCH {{gw}}/api/needs/{{needId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "The school has moved." }

### "What the group wanted to say" with income → 400 (rejected outright)
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/community-words
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "They said thank you for the income of 5000.", "dignityChecked": true }

### "What the group wanted to say" with a name → flagged by the Dignity Check (the coordinator must answer the flag before saving)
POST {{gw}}/api/bridge/dignity-check
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Ravi said he misses you, his income is 5000." }

### Cross-commitment Then and Now returns nothing for another user → { first: null, latest: null, sankalpas: [] }
### (the owner, {{vol}}, sees the seeded entry and Sankalpa; {{vol2}} and {{coord}} see nothing)
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/my-seva
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}

### Another volunteer reading a diary → empty list
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}

### The coordinator reading a diary → empty list
GET {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries?commitmentId={{commitmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}

### A userId in a diary body is ignored: saved under the caller ({{vol2}}), never {{vol}}
POST {{gw}}/api/reflect/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{vol2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "commitmentId": "{{commitmentId}}", "week": 2, "userId": "{{seededVolunteer}}", "text": "Not his words." }

### Needs search never returns more than 3
GET {{gw}}/api/needs?day=Saturday&maxKm=100&interest=teaching
Authorization: Bearer {{newvol}}

### Publishing without the read-back tick → 400
POST {{gw}}/api/needs
Authorization: Bearer {{coord}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Test", "want": "x", "serveUsWell": "x", "youWillLearn": "x", "groupSize": 5, "interestTags": ["teaching"],
  "rhythm": { "day": "Sunday", "start": "10:00", "end": "11:00" }, "weeks": 4, "place": "Test",
  "consent": { "readBack": false, "coordinatorConsent": true } }

### Every bridge job works with no key: run the four AI requests above with LLM_API_KEY unset → 200, source "fallback" or "rules"

### The dignity check flags "poor boy Ravi, income 5000": the "Dignity Check" request above (name, money, word we avoid)

### find-teaching returns only an id that is in verified wisdom, or null: compare its id with this list
GET {{gw}}/api/wisdom
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}

### Faking x-user-role from the browser does not grant coordinator access → still 403
POST {{gw}}/api/commitments/{{commitmentId}}/invitation
Authorization: Bearer {{vol}}
x-user-role: coordinator
x-user-id: {{coordinator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Inviting myself" }
